{{Basis}}
The '''Bachan calendar''' is a [[sunne]]an calendar made of 11 months divided into 30 days, except the last month which has 31 days, for a total of 331 days. Each month is divided into 3 weeks of 10 days. 

It went into effect in [[Qym]] following a royal decree issued by King [[Bacha I of Qym|Bacha I]] in {{abbr|1930|1603 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}. It was later adopted by other countries in [[Meran]] throughout the centuries and eventually throughout Basis following the [[SOME INTL TIME CONVENTION]] in {{abbr|2322|1929 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}. 

==Years==
To facilitate comparison of societal and technological progress with Earth's, and to make conversion straightforward, Year 1 of the Bachan calendar matches "Year 0.8307266177" of [[wikipedia:Earth|Earth]]'s [[wikipedia:Gregorian calendar|Gregorian calendar]]. In other words, every Basis Year equals 83.07% of an Earth Year<!--Earth Year divided by 0.8307266177 equals Basis Year-->. The years that follow can either be left as is, with just the number (Example: ''2440'') or add {{abbr|CE|Common Era}} after (Example: ''2440 CE''). The years that predate that epoch either use a negative sign before the year (Example: ''-2440'') or add {{abbr|BCE|Before Common Era}} after (Example: ''2440 BCE'').

This means that the Earth Year 2027 would equal the Basis Year 2440<!--2440.03256524--> (rounded). In a mirror manner, Basis Year 2400 would equal the Earth Year "1993.74388248", that is to say the start of the Basis Year 2400 was equivalent to September 29th, 1993. In the wiki, this will be written using the [[Template:abbr|abbreviation template]] as follow: 

:{{tlc|abbr|2400|1993.74 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}

Yielding: 

:<code>{{abbr|2400|1993.74 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}</code>

