Most religions on Basis have a designated one holy day during the week. In [[Sunneism]] and [[Mōnaïsm]], it is on the day of [[Mōna]], while in [[Scildism]] and [[Ānism]], it is on the day of [[Basis]]. In [[Manigism]], they do not have a weekly holy day, but rather celebrate the [[Last Day of the Year]] as their holy day, representing a new cycle. 

==Date format==
For wiki purposes, the English date format would be: 
*Neutral short format: dd/mm/yyyy (Example: ''14/05/2440'')
*Alternative short format: dd/w/mm/yyyy (Example: ''04/2/05/2440'')
*Neutral medium format: Day 'd' Month 'm' Year 'yyyy' (Example: ''Day 14 Month 5 Year 2440'')
*Alternative short format: Day 'd' Week 'w' Month 'm' Year 'yyyy' (Example: ''Day 4 Week 2 Month 5 Year 2440'')
*Neutral long format: 'd' day of the 'm' month in the year 'yyyy' (Example: ''14th day of the 5th month in the year 2440'')
*Alternative long format: 'd' day of the 'w' week of the 'm' month in the year 'yyyy' (Example: ''4th day of the 2nd week of the 5th month in the year 2440'')
*Scildist long format: 'd' day of the month of 'heroic name' in the year 'yyyy' (Example: ''14th day of the month of [[Nojed]] in the year 2440'')

